This same thing happened to me some time ago (my 223 HP Valkyrie choked
on a FORTUNE COOKIE! while leaving with the AMULET). I wrote to the net,
complaining bitterly, and received an explanation which is roughly as
follows:
(SPOILER ALERT)

	 Your maximum food capacity is 3000 (units).
	 Above 2000 you are satiated.
	 If you get to 2500 it asks you to "Continue eating? (yn)"
	 If you were below 2000 (ie: unsatiated) before you started
    eating, you can continue eating safely.
	 If you were above 2000 (ie: satiated) before you started
    eating, you will probably choke if you answer (y) to continue
    eating.
	 If you are already above 2500 when you begin to eat (your
    case, most probably), it doesn't even ask you, you just ckoke
    outright!

(DISCLAIMER: Any of the above values or facts(?) may be wrong, since I
didn't keep a copy of the original reply. These are just from vague
memory).

So, to be safe, if you want to eat a dragon or giant, teleport around
until you are not satiated. Then when it says "Continue eating?" you can
answer (y), and get your intrinsics, in complete safety.


